// RUN: check
// COMPILE-FAIL
// EXPECT-EXIT: 65
// CHECK-ERR: Cannot assign to const variable 'max'.
//
// Chapter 02 coverage: `const` forbids reassignment after initialization.
// Previously this diagnostic (K3002) was only raised by
// Compiler::compile_assignment in the backend (compiler.cc); the checker's
// TypeChecker::check_assign never inspected VarInfo::is_mutable on
// assignment, so `kinglet --check` silently exited 0 on this exact file.
// Fixed by adding the same K3002 check to check_assign — see the
// checker/backend divergence writeup in kinglet-lang/bootstrap#144. This
// case moved here from tests/exec/cases/const_reassign_rejected.kl (a
// RUN: run case written to document the gap before the fix) now that the
// checker catches it directly through the normal RUN: check pipeline.

int main() {
  const int max = 100;
  max = 200;
  return max;
}
